<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Drenthe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Drenthe is a province in the north-east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, with Assen as its capital. A thinly settled land of heath and peat, it is known for its prehistoric megalithic tombs, the hunebedden. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Utrecht, passing to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> in the 1530s. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> it had its own government but, unlike the seven provinces, no vote in the States General.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/drenthe.jpg" alt="Drenthe" width="320" height="361" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drenthe_in_the_Netherlands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
